---
import '../../../styles/finger-atlas-v4.css';
import '../../../styles/title-typography.css';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head><meta charset="utf-8" /><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1" /><meta name="description" content="A continuous, multiscale anatomical model of individual finger sensory and motor pathways." /><title>Finger Pathway Atlas V4 · Build the Simulation</title></head>
  <body>
    <main id="atlas-v4">
      <header class="atlas-top"><div><span class="atlas-edition">BUILD THE SIMULATION · ANATOMICAL EDITION IV</span><h1>Finger Pathway Atlas</h1></div><div class="top-actions"><a href="/simulations/finger-pathway-atlas/v3/" target="_top">V3 original</a><a href="/simulations/finger-pathway-atlas/references/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Reference plates ↗</a><button id="help-toggle" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="help-panel">About / controls</button><button id="fullscreen" aria-label="Enter full screen">⛶</button></div></header>
      <div class="atlas-workspace">
        <aside class="atlas-sidebar" aria-label="Explore anatomy">
          <div class="sidebar-title"><span>01 / EXPLORE</span><button id="overview">Whole anatomy</button></div>
          <nav id="region-list" aria-label="Anatomical regions"></nav>
          <section class="route-controls"><span class="eyebrow">02 / FOLLOW A PATHWAY</span><label for="route-kind">Pathway family</label><select id="route-kind"><option value="touch">Touch</option><option value="pain">Free endings / pain</option><option value="proprioception">Proprioception</option><option value="motor">Motor</option></select><label for="route-select">Individual modeled route</label><select id="route-select"></select><label class="check"><input type="checkbox" id="isolate" /> Isolate this route</label><div class="paired"><button id="previous">← Previous</button><button id="next">Next stop →</button></div></section>
          <details class="display-controls"><summary>Display & performance</summary><label for="quality">Detail budget</label><select id="quality"><option value="balanced">Balanced</option><option value="light">Light</option><option value="high">High detail</option></select><label class="check"><input type="checkbox" id="skin" checked /> Holographic skin</label><label class="check"><input type="checkbox" id="envelopes" checked /> Anatomical surfaces</label><label class="check"><input type="checkbox" id="supports" checked /> Cell support membranes</label><label class="check"><input type="checkbox" id="labels" checked /> Region labels</label><label class="check"><input type="checkbox" id="myelin" checked /> Myelin at close range</label><button id="export-map">Export cells & source map</button></details>
          <p class="sidebar-note">One spatial model. Every modeled cell keeps its identity as you move between scales.</p>
        </aside>
        <section class="atlas-stage" id="stage" aria-label="3D anatomical model">
          <canvas id="viewport" aria-label="Interactive 3D model. Drag to orbit, scroll to zoom, right-drag to pan." tabindex="0"></canvas>
          <div class="view-heading"><span id="view-eyebrow">CONTINUOUS ANATOMY / MILLIMETERS</span><h2 id="view-title">From fingertip to cortex</h2><p id="view-description">Intact anatomy, individually identified cells, connected pathways.</p><button id="inspect-region" class="inspect-region">Open V3 cell detail ↗</button></div>
          <section id="cortical-sections" hidden aria-label="Paired M1 and S1 coronal sections">
            <div class="cortex-toolbar">
              <div class="cortex-presets" aria-label="Cortical magnification">
                <button data-cortex-preset="gyrus">Two gyri</button><button data-cortex-preset="layers" aria-pressed="true">Six layers</button><button data-cortex-preset="deep">Layer VI + white matter</button><button data-cortex-preset="axon">Axon detail</button><button id="cortex-back">3D anatomy</button><button id="cortex-original">Selected V3 cell</button>
              </div>
              <div class="cortex-adjust"><label>Zoom both<input id="cortex-zoom" type="range" min="0" max="2.56" step=".01" value=".62" /></label><label>Depth / pan<input id="cortex-depth" type="range" min="-4" max="4" step=".01" value="0" /></label><label class="check"><input id="cortex-readable" type="checkbox" checked /> Visible fibers</label><label class="check"><input id="cortex-oblique" type="checkbox" /> Oblique 3D</label><label class="check"><input id="cortex-h01" type="checkbox" checked /> H01 neurites</label></div>
            </div>
            <div class="cortex-panes">
              {['M1 · PRIMARY MOTOR','S1 · PRIMARY SOMATOSENSORY'].map((name,i)=><div class="cortical-pane" aria-label={name}>
                <div class="cortex-pane-title"><strong>{name}</strong><span>{i===0?'Precentral gyrus · 3.4 mm cortical prior':'Postcentral gyrus · 2.2 mm cortical prior'}</span></div>
                <div class="cortex-layer-labels">{['I','II','III','IV','V','VI'].map((label,i)=><span data-layer={i}>L{label}</span>)}</div>
                <div class="cortex-pane-footer"><span class="cortex-tissue">Pia → I–VI → white matter</span><div class="cortex-scale"><i></i><span>1 mm</span></div><span class="cortical-source-status">H01 reference morphologies</span></div>
              </div>)}
            </div>
            <p class="cortex-caption"><span id="cortex-width-note"></span> <span>Separate modeled coronal planes · H01 is temporal cortex · drag to pan both</span> <a href="/simulations/finger-pathway-atlas/references/#cortical-methods" target="_blank" rel="noopener">H01, MRI & DKI sources ↗</a></p>
          </section>
          <div id="region-labels"></div>
          <div id="load-state" role="status"><span class="loading-dot"></span><span id="load-text">Preparing individual pathways…</span></div>
          <div id="fatal-error" role="alert" hidden><h2>The 3D viewer could not open</h2><p id="error-message"></p><button id="retry">Try again</button><a href="/simulations/finger-pathway-atlas/references/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the reference plates</a></div>
          <section class="cell-inspector" id="inspector" aria-label="Selected pathway">
            <div class="inspector-title"><span id="route-tag">MODELED TOUCH ROUTE</span><button id="clear-selection">Clear highlight</button><button id="inspector-toggle" aria-expanded="true">Collapse</button></div>
            <h3 id="route-title"></h3><div id="route-stops" aria-label="Pathway stops"></div>
            <div class="cell-row"><label for="cell-select">Cell identity</label><select id="cell-select"></select><button id="focus-cell">Inspect cell</button><button id="focus-ending">Inspect ending</button></div>
            <p id="cell-description"></p><p class="connection-note" id="connection-note"></p>
          </section>
          <footer class="scene-footer"><span id="scene-stats" role="status"></span><span id="scale-bar"><i></i><span></span></span><span class="gesture-hint">Drag · orbit &nbsp; Scroll · zoom &nbsp; Right-drag · pan</span></footer>
        </section>
      </div>
      <section id="help-panel" class="help-panel" hidden aria-label="About this model"><button id="help-close" aria-label="Close help">×</button><span class="eyebrow">VERSION 4 / MODEL SCOPE</span><h2>A complete route for every modeled cell.</h2><p>Choose a region, then use <strong>Inspect cell</strong> or <strong>Inspect ending</strong> to move from anatomy to cellular detail. Scroll back out to see where that same cell belongs. Next stop follows the selected route through its relay cells.</p><p>V4 integrates V3’s detailed cell models and the source anatomy, with the cortical display restricted to the left precentral and postcentral gyri into one millimeter coordinate system. Original membrane meshes load near the camera; distant cells retain their paths and identities. Detail budgets limit the number of visible objects, preserving the source geometry of each inspected model. Axons are lit cylindrical meshes at every viewing distance. A display-only radius floor keeps overview fibers readable; physical radii remain in the export. Use Cell support membranes to show or hide whole support structures around an ending; the cortex has its own paired coronal cross-section inspection mode. The scale bar measures the view plane through the camera target.</p><p>This is a representative, constructed circuit, <strong>not a complete biological census or an experimentally traced human connectome</strong>. Each synaptic relay is a different neuron. Sensory cells have a dorsal-root-ganglion soma; motor output bypasses that ganglion. Free-ending pathways cross in the spinal cord; touch and motor pathways cross separately in the medulla.</p><p>Histology and electron microscopy in the supplied comparison packet guide cell shapes, support cells, and endings. Those images span different species and tissues; they do not supply matched end-to-end reconstructions. V3’s measured human light-microscopy cortical traces remain available at their original scale. Their placement in S1/M1 and connection to these pathways is modeled. Selecting <strong>M1 + S1 coronal cortex</strong> opens both sections together. The paired cortical view adds six curved layers, a gray–white boundary and connected layer-VI projection examples. Twelve proofread H01 reference neurite trees (two from each layer) are reused in both gyri at their physical scale. H01 is temporal cortex; region placement and new long-range connections remain modeled. Layer V provides motor output, while the layer-VI examples continue toward thalamus. No electrical activity or biomechanical response is simulated.</p><p>Source anatomy: BodyParts3D / Anatomography, Database Center for Life Science, CC BY-SA 2.1 Japan; light overview surfaces with original V3 mesh detail loaded nearby. See the <a href="/assets/finger-pathway-atlas/v4/provenance.json" target="_blank" rel="noopener">V4 source record</a> and <a href="/simulations/finger-pathway-atlas/references/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">50 comparison plates</a>, plus the <a href="/assets/finger-pathway-atlas/v4/cortex-sources.json" target="_blank" rel="noopener">cortex source record</a>. Plate model panels show V3 and are retained as the development baseline.</p><p class="help-keys">Keyboard: <kbd>Home</kbd> whole anatomy · <kbd>←</kbd> / <kbd>→</kbd> pathway stops · <kbd>Escape</kbd> close this panel. Touch: one finger orbit, two fingers zoom/pan.</p></section>
      <div id="toast" role="status" hidden></div>
    </main>
    <script>import '../../../lib/finger-atlas-v4/viewer.js';</script>
  </body>
</html>
